// A port of llhttp 9.4.3 (https://github.com/nodejs/llhttp, MIT) — the HTTP/1.x parser Node 22.23.4
// bundles (process.versions.llhttp). It was written from 9.3.0's graph; what 9.4 added (the
// lenient_header_value_relaxed flag) is not reachable from Node, whose lenient flags stop at 0x200, and
// the http_parser fixtures recorded from Node 22.23.4 (including every byte in header names and values,
// URLs, reason phrases and chunk extensions) replay identically.
//
// llhttp is generated by llparse from a node graph (src/llhttp/http.ts, url.ts). This file follows
// that graph node by node, keeping llparse's execution rules so that callbacks, error codes, reasons
// and error positions match the C parser byte for byte:
//   - a "match" node needs one byte of input; when the buffer ends there the parser suspends in it
//   - "peek" edges do not consume, "match"/"select" edges do, "skipTo" consumes exactly one byte
//   - multi-byte sequences are matched as a trie; a mismatch half way goes to the node's otherwise
//     edge at the mismatching byte (the matched prefix stays consumed)
//   - a span start needs one byte of input; at the end of each execute() an open span is flushed to
//     its callback and restarted at the beginning of the next buffer
//   - errors record the position (error_pos); pauses record the node to resume at
// Only the spans and callbacks Node registers are kept (method/protocol/version spans and the
// *_complete callbacks other than chunk header/complete are null in Node's settings).

